{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch","id":1076944,"title":"Fae vs Spirits: making a sale pitch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T06:59:42-07:00","id":1076944,"title":"Fae vs Spirits: making a sale pitch","content":"Not sure if this is the correct thread but here is my question : how diferent is to cut a deal with a fae entity (changeling, goblin, fae lord, aspect of the wyrd ) from doing the same thing with Spirits ?<br /> I was thinking about making a campaign with mortal shamans (not awakened ) gaining power through bargains with entities from the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:10:08-07:00","id":1076981,"title":"","content":"I would say the main difference is that spirits are far more predictable, but harder to bind.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, while spirits in the same choir do have variants and differences, once you know it's a &quot;spirit of dogs&quot;, say, you've already learnt quite a lot about it. Maybe it will be more specific- &quot;dogs as predator&quot; or &quot;dogs as guardians&quot; or &quot;dogs as companions&quot;- but you know everything about it will be in some way related to &quot;dog&quot;.<br /> You can get some unpleasant surprises but overall, once you know what the spirits embodies ,you know what it wants and what it does. There's not much &quot;personality&quot; with a spirit- they don't really have preferences or quirks or beliefs beside what their resonance implies.<br /> <br /> A True Fae, on the other hand, is far more unpredictable. Learning a title doesn't help in the same way as learning a spirit's resonance does. It's other titles don't necessarily need to have anything to do with each other, and even then they're more themes then anything else. The Bearer of Fire can appear as a brutish flame-beast, a sneaky arsonist or a wise bringer of enlightenment depending on its current story, and even that's lost if it switches to its other title of &quot;the Queen of Locusts&quot;. Each fae is an individual, and you need to be prepared for anything.<br /> The same for other Fae creatures- changelings are ex-humans and have all the variety of humans, and goblins encompass dozens of sentient species. Each one is an individual that you need to get to know to bargain with<br /> <br /> On the other hand, unless you have a specific power, your bargain with a spirit is just a standard bargain. If the spirit decides the deal isn't in its best interest any more, it's perfectly capable of taking back its power there and then. Once you've made a bargain, you need to ensure that the spirit keeps a good reason to work with you. (on the flip side, you can also betray the spirit if that helps you).<br /> <br /> The Fae can't. If you've made a full Pact with them, they can't break their word, not without something terrible happening. There can be loophole abuse and technicalities, but if a Fae creature promises not to attack you it won't attack you regardless of how convenient it is. The flip side is that you are also bound if the Fae is even remotely competent.<br /> <br /> TL;DR- spirits are easier to deal with but potentially treacherous. The Fae are unpredictable but once a bargain is struck are more reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:13:59-07:00","id":1076982,"title":"","content":"Fae are also older, have more experience in making deals and exploiting loopholes and thus far harder to please","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:15:25-07:00","id":1076985,"title":"","content":"A changeling is most likely to give you very small, but possibly supernatural benefits, which make your life convenient for little more than a symbolic cost. What they offer pretty much has to be what they're capable of, in their free time, with minimal cost. The main things changelings want is connections to other humans which make the huntsmen overlook them.<br /> <br /> Goblins are like back alley thieves trying to sell you wonder on the cheap. Their contracts aren't usually that strong, but they're bloody useful and straightforward ways to get what you want... but have a tendency to explode - their drawbacks suck, and the Goblins don't have to warn you about it. All they ask for, though, are abstract qualities you probably won't miss: last night's dream, a memory from infancy, your first crush, your last regret.<br /> <br /> The True Fae beget terror. What they want is captives (escaped changelings or new ones ) and glamour. They may ask you to place an innocuous item under someones pillow (to poison their dreams), or to &quot;scare&quot; some one (removing a changelings layer of defense), or may just harvest one of your emotions to leave your soul empty. No matter how innocent it seems, though, they'll use it in a way you'll probably find evil: kidnapping people, driving them insane, maybe making fey monsters from your emotions.... You might not see the results. Maybe. But they do love toying with people. The plus side? Magic is cheap for them they can do almost anything and think nothing of it. And if your request requires they enter the mortal world, why then you have to sustain them while they're here, and they get all kinds of access that wasn't part of the deal...<br /> <br /> You have to be fae to make a contract with the Wyrd and it requires a truly epic task to make a new one. If you can get in on that, though, its super straightforward to use. &quot;Goblin vows&quot; are a lot like bargaining with spirits, actually: do something which enhances the Aspect, it does an equivalent power for you. Contracts are even mores structured: pay glamour and/or this minor cost, get this specific thing. <br /> <br /> Spirits are usually more straightforward than any fae. They want essence, protection from other spirits, or access to earth to shape their influences. If you set it up right, you can do minor favors in their purview (feed stray cats, never hide from the rain, always keep a flame in your house) to maintain a relationship, then do a ritual that generates essence to ask them to use their power. Unfortunately, you have to find the right spirit, and you may have to talk down a vastly more powerful being fron the insane things it demands (stop a forest from being developed, destroy the most popular business in town, give them a human to possess). You'll always be weaker than a spirit, so need to really know your stuff to negotiate, and that knowledge isn't very easy to get.<br /> (And that's if werewolves aren't part of the setting. If they are, you're always going to be at risk for pissing off one of them accidentally)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:28:48-07:00","id":1076989,"title":"","content":"The biggest difference is that while both spirits and fae are oath-happy otherworldly beings with a tenuous-at-best grasp of the human mindset outside of established grifts, the fae operate at a greater remove from material reality by default and have a much more scattershot distribution of power and intelligence compared to spirits. A spirit acting out-of-sorts with its portfolio is evidence of a weird exception of its circumstances or a hidden facet of its nature, and the creatures whose Rank affords them the treatment of nobility tend to be more approachable than the beasts-and-children demographic they treat as resources, but a substantial number of fae are dissembling and/or treacherous just by virtue of being both closer to and further from humanity.<br /> <br /> Spiritual resources are almost exclusively additive, which is part of why more powerful spirits tend to feed by proxy through their lessers, but pretty much every pixie, nixie, goblin and djinn can give or take goods and services of wildly varying levels of abstraction in based on criteria that only make sense to them and the Wyrd. Meanwhile, if a spirit is intelligent enough to ask you for something that's not within its immediate purviews and has no obvious relation to feeding it, the first explanation (besides the above bit about hidden variables) is that Politics is happening and it needs to blight a rival or curry favor from an ally.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of active lifespan to consider; most spirits tend to be persistent consequences of significant objects and events, but almost all fae hail from a place where dreams populate the wilderness and the rules making immediate sense is lower on the world's priorities than prices being paid and aesthetics being consistent \u2014 self-preservation is paramount in the Shadow and hit-or-miss in the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:44:02-07:00","id":1076998,"title":"","content":"Also, a spirit wants essence. That's all a spirit wants, ever- no matter how complex its plans are, they all boil down to &quot;get essence&quot;. This makes spirits comparatively simple to deal with and approach- can you get it essence? Then it's listening. If not it's not. Likewise, if the spirit doesn't think it can gain essence by attacking you, it won't attack. Spirits have simple motivations that you can easily exploit if you know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> A True Fae doesn't have that. Arguably, it wants &quot;a story&quot; but that is far vaguer and harder to exploit then wanting &quot;essence&quot;, and it seems they do have other motivations and goals anyway. Changelings and goblins, of course, have all the variety of any human in what they want, fear and need. With a Fae creature it's a lot harder to come up with a &quot;sales pitch&quot;, at least in the same generic way you can with spirits. You can't just offer glamour and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:19:09-07:00","id":1077016,"title":"","content":"Spirits are more complex then just feed me essence.<br /> <br /> Spirits can be motivated by issues of survival, fear of predators, essence, and so on.<br /> <br /> They are also influenced by spirit politics, rank, status in their Chorus, not wanting to become a Magath, ect...<br /> <br /> Nature, a Spirit of Charity will never to be greedy, its too antithetical to their nature.<br /> <br /> And then there are the weird spirits, spirits of the void, Igiam, Mage Spirits, Purified, half spirits like Werewolves, odder stuff that bucks the usual trends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:59:30-07:00","id":1077041,"title":"","content":"Well, the Fae seem bound by their deals as a core aspect of their nature. Spirits, while usually less skilled at deception and dishonesty (except if that is their type) are not thus bound, unless it is in their Ban somewhere.<br /> <br /> Spirits may be easier to contact, being more &quot;near&quot; than the Hedge (Twilight <i>is</i> in the same world. Their motives are also fairly easy to infer as well (Essence, Essence, and Essence). Fae may have odd and greatly varying requirements. Glamour is common, but they don't need and focus on it quite like spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:01:35-07:00","id":1077043,"title":"","content":"Ok guys, thank you all for answering. I think the cheapest way to get what I want is to adapt this template into something more animist:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\"> Minor/Micro Template: Hedge Sorcerers - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, for those who want a little mortal-Changeling magic in their games, here's a Mortal+ template, using the released Playtest rules so far. Hedge Sorcerers are </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Still, I will consider all your imput about spirit 's psychology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:38:59-07:00","id":1077061,"title":"","content":"Spirits will often only care about the immediate consequences of a deal -- what they're giving and getting. Many fae (and not just the Gentry!) care about agreements and promises for their own sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:42:01-07:00","id":1077064,"title":"","content":"Fae, though not necessarily goblins, always struck me as being open to deals, almost wanting them, I suppose? Or intrigued enough by the idea that they might be take one up.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't seem to care so much, especially as you go up in rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:34:43-07:00","id":1077094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1077061#post1077061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits will often only care about the immediate consequences of a deal -- what they're giving and getting. Many fae (and not just the Gentry!) care about agreements and promises for their own sake.</div> </div> </div> </div> So for Spirits deals are just a business transaction, a means to an ends, for the Fae it's both means and ends and far more significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:41:28-07:00","id":1077097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1077043#post1077043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok guys, thank you all for answering. I think the cheapest way to get what I want is to adapt this template into something more animist:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edge-sorcerers</a><br /> <br /> Still, I will consider all your imput about spirit 's psychology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If you aren't including Changeling, all you have to do is change some words around and say the Contracts are from bargaining with spirits. There's enough conceptual overlap that there shouldn't be any major issues.<br /> <br /> You could also just use outright spirit powers for a character, similar to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages\">here</a>. Only real issue is XP costs and figuring out how to get enough Essence. You can sorta side-step the XP costs using @Arcanist's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone\">Pacts</a> framework.<br /> <br /> Nevermind: You are already aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-12-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:26:26-07:00","id":1077169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1076981#post1076981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, unless you have a specific power, your bargain with a spirit is just a standard bargain. If the spirit decides the deal isn't in its best interest any more, it's perfectly capable of taking back its power there and then. Once you've made a bargain, you need to ensure that the spirit keeps a good reason to work with you. (on the flip side, you can also betray the spirit if that helps you).<br /> <br /> The Fae can't. If you've made a full Pact with them, they can't break their word, not without something terrible happening. There can be loophole abuse and technicalities, but if a Fae creature promises not to attack you it won't attack you regardless of how convenient it is. The flip side is that you are also bound if the Fae is even remotely competent.<br /> <br /> TL;DR- spirits are easier to deal with but potentially treacherous. The Fae are unpredictable but once a bargain is struck are more reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm... Not sure about that. Many aspects from Werewolf 's rituals like chiminaje are based on ancient agreements stuck back when Pangea. Even with Father Wolf dead and thus unable to enforce rules, spirits are still bound to them. <br /> Of course, maybe any of this would be of no use to a mortal occultist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 04-12-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:40:10-07:00","id":1077184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1077064#post1077064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits don't seem to care so much, especially as you go up in rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, spirits are roughly as concerned with oaths as the average fae is \u2014 rites are empowered by deals with powerful spirits, and interacting with the more ground-level manifestation of that framework has been part of the Elodoth's niche for quite some time. (I can't remember which book it was, but I distinctly remember a spiritual counterpart to Geist's note that ghosts typically keep to their end of a bargain, and even without that note <i>gathra</i> is consistent enough as a means of exchange that offerings to a spirit aren't called out as a particularly risky endeavor.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:46:06-07:00","id":1077187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1077184#post1077184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, spirits are roughly as concerned with oaths as the average fae is \u2014 rites are empowered by deals with powerful spirits, and interacting with the more ground-level manifestation of that framework has been part of the Elodoth's niche for quite some time. (I can't remember which book it was, but I distinctly remember a spiritual counterpart to Geist's note that ghosts typically keep to their end of a bargain, and even without that note <i>gathra</i> is consistent enough as a means of exchange that offerings to a spirit aren't called out as a particularly risky endeavor.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In following my statement of belief that Fae were 'interested' in oaths, and might take one up on a whim even if it didn't have to, with many changeling origins starting as such, I was referring to their overall interest in initiating oaths. Rites and other things have become sort of rules of the Hisil, but spirits aren't usually approaching with intent to deal with any werewolf or mortal who wants something and is willing to trade for it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure when they do make their oaths they generally keep to them, but getting to that point is trickier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:15:24-07:00","id":1079988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1076944-fae-vs-spirits-making-a-sale-pitch?p=1076982#post1076982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fae are also older</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly Debateable, in my opinion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 04-20-2017, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,",